1. **An automated storage and retrieval system comprising:**

a plurality of storage racks, each storage rack having a plurality of vertically spaced storage levels and a plurality of storage locations disposed along each storage level;

a plurality of picking aisles defined between respective adjacent storage racks;

a plurality of level decks associated with the respective storage levels, each level deck providing a travel surface that communicates between at least two of the picking aisles;

at least one automated picking vehicle configured to travel along the level decks and through the picking aisles and to retrieve items from the storage locations; and

a controller configured to direct the automated picking vehicle along a picking route through a selected one of the picking aisles and to perform a plurality of item picks from respective storage locations during a common traversal of the selected picking aisle,

wherein the storage racks bordering the selected picking aisle have coordinated spacing of the respective storage locations along a longitudinal direction of the selected picking aisle such that the respective storage locations for the plurality of item picks are sequentially accessible to the automated picking vehicle without the automated picking vehicle exiting and reentering the selected picking aisle.
